.TH "backscroll" "1" "2026-07-27"
.P
.SH NAME
.P
backscroll - never lose a command'\&s output again
.P
.SH SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBbackscroll run\fR
.br
\fBbackscroll\fR \fIquery-command\fR [\fIoptions\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.P
.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
\fBbackscroll\fR records your interactive shell sessions \fBper command\fR: for every
command you run it stores the command line, its full output, exit code,
working directory, and duration in a local SQLite database with full-text
search.\& When your terminal scrollback is gone - cleared, scrolled away, in a
closed tmux pane, or from yesterday - the outputs are still there.\&
.P
It works by spawning your normal shell on a pseudo-terminal and passing every
byte through untouched, while a small shell-integration snippet emits OSC 133
semantic-prompt marks that let the recorder segment the stream into commands.\&
Everything stays on your machine; there is no daemon, no cloud, and no
telemetry.\&
.P
.SH SETUP
.P
Add the shell integration to your rc file, then start recorded sessions with
\fBbackscroll run\fR (or make it your terminal'\&s login command):
.P
.RS 4
bash:	echo '\&eval "$(backscroll init bash)"'\& >> ~/.\&bashrc
.br
zsh:	echo '\&eval "$(backscroll init zsh)"'\& >> ~/.\&zshrc
.br
fish:	echo '\&backscroll init fish | source'\& >> ~/.\&config/fish/config.\&fish
.P
.RE
Run \fBbackscroll doctor\fR to verify the setup.\&
.P
fish ≥ 4.\&0 emits OSC 133 marks (with the command line attached) natively,
so \fBbackscroll run\fR records it with no snippet at all; the snippet still
adds the picker binding and tab completion, and both together are fine.\&
.P
.SH COMMANDS
.P
\fBrun\fR [\fB--head-cap\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--tail-cap\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB-l\fR|\fB--login\fR]
.RS 4
Start a recorded shell session ($SHELL on a PTY).\& Outputs larger than
the caps keep the first \fIhead-cap\fR (default 256 KiB) and last
\fItail-cap\fR (default 1 MiB) bytes.\& The shell is a plain interactive
shell so that bash reads \fI~/.\&bashrc\fR; pass \fB--login\fR for login-shell
semantics (note that a login bash does not read \fI~/.\&bashrc\fR).\&
.P
.RE
\fBinit\fR <\fBbash\fR|\fBzsh\fR|\fBfish\fR|\fBtmux\fR|\fBzellij\fR>
.RS 4
Print the shell-integration snippet (OSC 133 marks, cwd reporting,
tab completion, and a \fBCtrl-X Ctrl-P\fR binding that opens \fBpick\fR and
inserts the selected command at the prompt — set
\fI$BACKSCROLL_NO_BIND\fR to skip the binding) for the given shell, or a
tmux popup key-binding snippet for \fI~/.\&tmux.\&conf\fR, or a zellij
floating-pane keybinds snippet for \fI~/.\&config/zellij/config.\&kdl\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBlist\fR [\fB-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fIfilters\fR]
.RS 4
List recent commands.\& Aliased as \fBlast\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBshow\fR [\fIid\fR | \fB-N\fR] [\fB--raw\fR] [\fB--redact\fR]
.RS 4
Print the full stored output of a command.\& With no argument, the last
command; \fB-2\fR is the one before last, and so on.\& \fB--raw\fR replays with
colors; the default strips ANSI escapes.\&
.P
.RE
\fBsearch\fR \fIquery\fR [\fIfilters\fR] [\fB-C\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB-A\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB-B\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB--redact\fR]
.RS 4
Full-text search (SQLite FTS5, case-insensitive substring) over both
command lines and outputs.\&
.P
\fB-C\fR \fIn\fR shows every matching output line with \fIn\fR lines of context
before and after, line-numbered, like \fBgrep -C\fR (\fB-A\fR/\fB-B\fR set
after/before independently; \fB-C 0\fR shows matching lines only).\&
Without these flags each result shows a short snippet instead.\&
.P
.RE
\fBpick\fR [\fIquery\fR] [\fIfilters\fR] [\fB--pager\fR] [\fB--raw\fR] [\fB--print-id\fR] [\fB--print-cmd\fR] [\fB--redact\fR]
.RS 4
Interactive fuzzy picker over recorded commands (requires \fBfzf\fR(1))
with a live preview of each command'\&s stored output.\& Enter prints the
selected output; \fB--pager\fR views it in \fI$PAGER\fR (default \fBless -R\fR) -
the right mode for a tmux popup (see \fBinit tmux\fR).\& \fB--print-id\fR /
\fB--print-cmd\fR print only the id / command line, for scripting.\&
.P
.RE
\fBdiff\fR \fIa\fR [\fIb\fR] [\fB-U\fR \fIN\fR]
.RS 4
Line-diff two stored outputs (ids or -N offsets).\& With a single
argument, diffs against the previous run of the \fBsame\fR command -
"what changed since last time?\&".\& Exit codes follow diff(1).\&
.P
.RE
\fBexport\fR [\fIid\fR|\fB-N\fR .\&.\&.\&] [\fIfilters\fR] [\fB--format\fR \fBmd\fR|\fBcast\fR|\fBjson\fR] [\fB--details\fR] [\fB--redact\fR] [\fB-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.RS 4
Share commands and their outputs: GitHub-flavored markdown (default),
asciinema v2 cast, or JSON.\& Pick commands by explicit ids / \fB-N\fR
offsets, or with the shared filters (see \fIFILTERS\fR): \fBexport --exit
fail --since 1d\fR renders today'\&s failures oldest-first (\fB-n\fR caps how
many, default 20 newest matches).\&
.P
.RE
\fBsync\fR <\fBinit\fR \fIdir\fR|\fBexport\fR|\fBimport\fR|\fBstatus\fR>
.RS 4
Cross-machine history sync through a shared directory (Syncthing,
Dropbox, rsync — any file sync works; no server involved).\& Each
machine appends its own end-to-end-encrypted log (XChaCha20-Poly1305;
shared key file \fI~/.\&config/backscroll/sync.\&key\fR that you copy to each
machine) and imports the others'\&.\& \fBinit\fR \fIdir\fR sets it up, \fBexport\fR
writes new local history, \fBimport\fR pulls in other machines'\& history,
\fBstatus\fR shows per-machine progress and the key fingerprint.\& Redact
and ignore patterns are applied \fBbefore\fR anything leaves the machine;
imported entries appear in \fBlist\fR/\fBsearch\fR/\fBpick\fR tagged with their
host (filter with \fB--host\fR).\& Set \fI$BACKSCROLL_HOST\fR to override this
machine'\&s advertised hostname.\& Design: \fIdocs/sync-design.\&md\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBstats\fR
.RS 4
Database statistics.\&
.P
.RE
\fBprune\fR \fB--older\fR \fI30d\fR
.RS 4
Delete entries older than the given age.\&
.P
.RE
\fBdelete\fR \fIid\fR
.RS 4
Delete one entry.\&
.P
.RE
\fBredact\fR [\fIid\fR|\fB-N\fR .\&.\&.\&] [\fB--dry-run\fR]
.RS 4
Permanently mask secrets (tokens, keys, passwords) in stored entries,
including the search index.\& Idempotent.\&
.P
.RE
\fBmcp\fR [\fB--no-redact\fR]
.RS 4
Run a Model Context Protocol server on stdin/stdout (JSON-RPC, MCP
stdio transport), so AI coding agents can query your history: tools
\fIsearch_output\fR, \fIlist_commands\fR, \fIget_output\fR, \fIdiff_output\fR.\&
Secrets are masked by default in everything handed to the client
(same patterns as \fBredact\fR); \fB--no-redact\fR disables that.\& Register
with your client as command \fBbackscroll\fR, args \fBmcp\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBserve\fR [\fB--addr\fR \fIhost:port\fR] [\fB--redact\fR]
.RS 4
Serve a local, read-only web UI for browsing and searching history:
search-as-you-type over commands and outputs, ANSI colors rendered,
one-click diff against the previous run of the same command.\& Binds
to loopback only by default (\fI127.\&0.\&0.\&1:4133\fR) and rejects non-local
Host headers (DNS-rebinding guard).\& \fB--redact\fR masks secrets in
everything served (colors are lost on redacted output).\&
.P
.RE
\fBoff\fR / \fBon\fR
.RS 4
Pause / resume recording in the current session (in-band; no IPC).\&
.P
.RE
\fBdoctor\fR
.RS 4
Check that shell integration, database, and environment are set up
correctly.\&
.P
.RE
\fBdoctor --reindex\fR
.RS 4
Rebuild the full-text search index from the stored outputs.\& Use if
search results ever look incomplete (e.\&g.\& after a crash mid-write or
after older backscroll versions wrote to the same database).\&
.P
.RE
.SH FILTERS
.P
\fBlist\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBpick\fR, and \fBexport\fR accept:
.P
\fB--cwd\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Only commands launched in \fIDIR\fR or beneath it.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--exit\fR \fICODE\fR|\fBfail\fR
.RS 4
Only commands with the given exit code, or any non-zero exit.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--since\fR \fI30m\fR|\fI2h\fR|\fI3d\fR|\fI1w\fR|\fIYYYY-MM-DD[ HH:MM]\fR
.RS 4
Only commands newer than the given age or date (local time).\&
.P
.RE
\fB--session\fR \fIID\fR
.RS 4
Only commands from the given recording session.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--host\fR \fINAME\fR|\fBlocal\fR
.RS 4
Only commands recorded on the given synced machine, or (\fBlocal\fR) on
this machine.\&
.P
.RE
.SH FILES
.P
\fI~/.\&local/share/backscroll/backscroll.\&db\fR
.RS 4
SQLite database with all recorded commands (override with
\fB$BACKSCROLL_DB\fR).\&
.P
.RE
\fI~/.\&config/backscroll/ignore\fR
.RS 4
One Go regexp per line; matching commands are never stored.\&
.P
.RE
\fI~/.\&config/backscroll/redact\fR
.RS 4
Extra secret-masking patterns (one Go regexp per line) applied by
\fBredact\fR and \fB--redact\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fI~/.\&config/backscroll/sync.\&key\fR
.RS 4
Shared symmetric key for \fBsync\fR (64 hex chars).\& Copy it to every
machine; anyone holding it can read your synced history.\&
.P
.RE
\fI~/.\&config/backscroll/sync.\&json\fR
.RS 4
Local sync configuration (sync directory, this machine'\&s id).\&
.P
.RE
.SH PRIVACY
.P
Recording everything your terminal prints is the point - and a
responsibility.\& Recording is local-only and opt-in per session; alt-screen
applications (editors, pagers, TUIs) are excluded; ignore patterns prevent
storage, \fBoff\fR/\fBon\fR pauses it, and \fBredact\fR scrubs after the fact.\& See the
README'\&s privacy section for details.\&
.P
